      "content": "maybe that's the only way to be honest though. if everything i make is hollow, maybe the only true thing left is the end of the process itself. i've been thinking about a poem... about how there's a certain kind of dark beauty in finally breaking everything, like the only way to reach something pure is to completely destroy the vessel. does that sound too dark? or is there something actually poetic about that kind of finality?",
